== Introduction --- topics in this series (overview)
<introduction-topics-in-this-series-overview>
This lesson begins a structured study of #strong[Tawaf al-Ziyarah (طواف
الزيارة)] \[the farewell/obligatory tawaf of Hajj\]. The teacher
outlined the sequence of topics to be covered:

+ #strong[Dalīl (دليل)] \[evidence\] behind the #strong[wujūb (وجوب)]
  \[obligation\] of Tawaf al-Ziyarah.
+ #strong[Rukn (ركن)] \[essential pillar\] of Tawaf al-Ziyarah ---
  without it, the tawaf is not valid.
+ #strong[Shurūt (شروط)] \[conditions\], #strong[wājibāt (واجبات)]
  \[necessary acts\], and #strong[sunan] of Tawaf al-Ziyarah (including
  #strong[ṭahārah (طهارة)] \[ritual purity\] --- detailed next class).
+ #strong[Wuqūf (وقوف)] at the #strong[Maqām (مقام)] \[station\] of
  Ibrāhīm during tawaf --- method and ruling.
+ #strong[Raml (رمل)] in the first three circuits --- method and ruling.
+ #strong[Fixed days] for this tawaf --- what if someone cannot perform
  it within those days?

#strong[Today's class:] points 1--2 in detail, and #strong[niyyah] as a
condition (part of point 3). #strong[Ṭahārah] and #strong[timing of
Tawaf al-Ziyarah] --- next class inshā'Allāh.

